{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"partSymbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPartSymbol","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<part-symbol>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"partSymbol","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAttributesV10partSymbolAA07MXLPartE0VSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"partSymbol"},"abstract":[{"text":"The part-symbol element indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/partSymbol","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/partsymbol"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartSymbol":{"title":"MXLPartSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part-symbol type indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score; brace is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default value. The top-staff and bottom-staff attributes are used when the brace does not extend across the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire part. For example, in a 3-staff organ part, the top-staff will typically be 1 for the right hand, while"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the bottom-staff will typically be 2 for the left hand. Staff 3 for the pedals is usually outside the brace."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"By default, the presence of a part-symbol element that does not extend across the entire part also indicates a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corresponding change in the common barlines within a part."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes/partSymbol":{"abstract":[{"text":"The part-symbol element indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score.","type":"text"}],"title":"partSymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/partSymbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/partsymbol","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"partSymbol"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV","text":"MXLPartSymbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"title":"MXLAttributes","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}